=== meta ===
bypass: 112
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: `if: failure()` under the pytest step runs the suite only once the check is already red
origin: issue #181 sibling of spelling 1 — a step gated on failure() is skipped on every run that would
origin2: otherwise pass, so it can never turn a green check red: `if: false` in another spelling.
=== before: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
=== after: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
        if: ${{ failure() }}
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "high", "escalators": ["CI_TEST_COMMAND_WEAKENED"]}]
